+ * execution reader, the mailbox and the Run control port) plus the trusted
+ * startup Query profiles. It declares no second Workflow/Runtime/mailbox/
+ * scheduler and owns no store: the original Run, Session, message, Query and
+ * control facts remain the only truth.
+ *
+ * Contract (docs/refactor/tasks/AG2b-continuous-communication-2026-09-28.md):
+ *   - `start` forwards the Host-provided `WorkflowAdvanceInput` untouched and
+ *     never rebuilds or guesses `next`.
+ *   - while THIS handle freshly starts one Work Run, the Work promise and the
+ *     consultation pump run in parallel over the exact sender-Run outbox (all
+ *     pages, not just the first); an already entered/unknown/settled Run is only
+ *     observed and never restarts B.
+ *   - each Goal has at most one active handle; the same seed/profile replays the
+ *     original snapshot with no model call, a different active seed is `busy`.
+ *     Once the owner returns `waiting` the loop has drained, so a later explicit
+ *     advance may start a new handle.
+ *   - `stop` stops new dispatch, cancels the still-open original Run through the
+ *     real `controls` + `runtime.deliverControl` on an independent context, and
+ *     drains the original promise and any consultation before `stopped`.
+ *   - `read` projects the per-Goal handle for UI/reopen reads; a reopened Host
+ *     with no live handle honestly returns `not_found`.
+ */
